ew and packed browser evidence remain separate, with their stated limitations.\n\nThe exact pointer regression test patch applies strictly to d648 in an isolated index and yields autocomplete spec SHA c049c617e9a3dc7f59c6383d0391e6d59813f5b6ca72374db3c3082e1f8b1683. The author reports that source and test landed at 45bbb3016f631296c08cf0eaa5f54a0e61455cf1; that landing report is not substituted for this afterimage check.\n\nThe prospective inventory patch strictly applies to the seven-row candidate inventory a0393aef3f69f908647b6e31e7039c12f97549e2ec7b14fa35a9688edd516906 and produces 1f9c82d0dc6560eee416661faa2ecc0732c7e9ece34b323645371bfa1ee5f2f1. Exactly the autocomplete row changes: its previous complete row is preserved as the new previous snapshot, prior snapshots are retained, candidate hash is c049c617..., and goldens, execution claims, all other rows and root metadata are unchanged. This is valid only on that exact baseline and source afterimage. No tagged browser run is claimed. The fixed archived 2228 probe remains unchanged; a separate current-epoch coordinated run and individually reviewed per-SHA evidence remain necessary.\n"
